# CQ 15: Which protocols do the entities employ?
#
# Clause 5.2.3 defines the protocol as the rules governing the exchange between
# peer entities. Where question 14 reports the vertical relation, this one
# reports what governs the horizontal one.
#
# Reported per protocol rather than per entity, so the entities sharing one
# appear together. Two peer entities employing the same protocol is the normal
# case and the reason the concept exists: 5.2.3 has peer entities communicate
# by a protocol they both follow.
#
# A protocol employed by one entity alone is worth noticing. Either the peer is
# not modelled, or the model states a rule that nothing on the other side
# follows.
PREFIX iso7498: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso7498#>
SELECT ?protocol (COUNT(DISTINCT ?entity) AS ?entityCount)
       (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?entityName; separator=", ") AS ?entities)
WHERE {
  ?entity iso7498:employsProtocol ?p .
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?p), ".*#", "") AS ?protocol)
  BIND(REPLACE(STR(?entity), ".*#", "") AS ?entityName)
} GROUP BY ?protocol ORDER BY ?protocol
